# Wave W17-AB (Route 223): league rock — cliff-foot rock: a dark basalt boulder standing in the deep lane, its joints drawn VERTICAL like the Summit cliff it fell from, foam collar at its base (design: the lane runs to the League cliff; the cliff’s own jointing is columnar, and its foot rocks keep the family habit). Route 223’s own rock — split from Route 220’s swell rock by jointing entire (cliff-vertical vs swell-worn smooth) and from Foamline’s shallows rock by depth: this stone stands in deep shadowed water, that one in bright shallows.
